  "reading": "DEGENERATE, AND THE EDGE SHARPENS -- from 2x32 onward the return-optimal policy can do no better than stop at the source, V*(s0) equal to log R(s0) exactly, so the MDP the reduction produces has a trivial optimum. Meanwhile the reduction itself stays exact, KL at lambda = 1 below 1e-15 at every scale, and the price of a ten percent error in the coefficient grows from 0.0339 to 0.3852 nats. All of the GFlowNet sits in the coefficient being exactly one, and a return-maximising rule has nothing to aim at."
